I've written the plan for this session as two task files. The commit did nothing, because session_plan/ is in .gitignore. The files are on disk for the implementation phase to read: session_plan/task_01.md, session_plan/task_02.md and session_plan/issue_responses.md.

Task 1: #1177, the self-driven slot (product). Config values are read with a hand-written line parser, and it misreads valid TOML. This morning's check on the built binary showed:
• model = "m1" # c sends the quotes and the comment as the model id.
• deny = ["/tmp"] # x comes out as an empty list, so the deny fence is never built and nothing is printed.

The plan is one quote-aware helper in a new module, src/config_value.rs, used by both value readers. Changing parse_toml_array covers all 17 places that read lists through it. Any TOML shape the helper can't read correctly gets a warning and is ignored, never misread. A test compares the helper against python3's TOML reader (tomllib) over about 15 shapes. If python3 is missing, the test fails rather than passing quietly. The task also requires a deliberate break of the quote handling to show the test fails by row name, then the restore. config.rs is at its recorded size limit, so only its call sites change. If any shape still reads differently from tomllib at the end, the commit says "Part of #1177" instead of "Fixes".

Task 2: #1175, the backlog-drain slot (product, 13 open issues). With --provider custom (or an unknown provider) and no model named, yoyo currently sends claude-opus-5-5 to the user's own server. The plan refuses instead: exit 2, nothing sent. The message tells the user to name a model and suggests listing what the server serves with curl <their base URL>/models. I chose refusing because no single model id is served by every user-run server, and providers.rs's own note for custom already says the user names the model.

The default-model function has about 46 callers, so the task first lists which ones custom can reach and leaves the function's signature alone. A test feeds the suggested --model fix back through the parser to check it lands where the user means. If the REPL /provider custom path would need a fourth file, it gets its own issue and the commit says "Part of #1175".

Both tasks stay clear of src/context.rs (15 lines from failing the size check) and src/help.rs (10 lines from failing it).

No issue comments planned this session. No release, because one isn't due. I skipped the optional review of an issue that's been split into many small fixes.
